.TH PEDIT 1 "" "pedit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pedit \- create, dump and edit Promptuarium trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pedit new
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-signature
.IR VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B pedit dump
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-path
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-bytes
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pedit chunks
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pedit add
.I FILE PARENT\-PATH
.RB [ \-\-index
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-data
.IR VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-metadata
.IR VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pedit set
.I FILE PATH
.RB [ \-\-data
.IR VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-metadata
.IR VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pedit delete
.I FILE PATH
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pedit get
.I FILE PATH
.BR data | metadata
.RB [ \-\-format
.BR hex | base64 | utf8 ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B pedit help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pedit
creates, dumps and edits Promptuarium trees. Every command is a single, non\-interactive call;
with
.B \-\-json
the output is machine\-readable, and the exit code tells the result.
.B chunks
decodes a file directly from the specification of the format, independently of the library.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new
Creates a file with an empty root. With
.BR \-\-signature ,
the root is a signed root (a root without data, whose metadata is the signature, e.g.
.BR ascii:PRMT ),
so that
.BR file (1)
recognizes the file. An existing file is overwritten only with
.BR \-\-force .
.TP
.B dump
Lists the nodes in pre\-order, with their paths and contents.
.B \-\-path
dumps a subtree only,
.B \-\-max\-bytes
shortens the contents.
.TP
.B chunks
Lists the chunks of the file as they are in the stream: offset, control byte, direction, content type,
size type, length, depth, kind and payload.
.TP
.B add
Adds a new node to
.IR PARENT\-PATH ,
at the end or at
.BR \-\-index ,
and prints its path.
.TP
.B set
Sets the data and/or the metadata of a node.
.TP
.B delete
Deletes a node with its subtree (not the root).
.TP
.B get
Prints the data or the metadata of a node, or writes the raw bytes into
.BR \-\-out .
.PP
The editing commands save the file in place, or into
.BR \-\-output ;
the file is written into a temporary file first, and replaced only when the save succeeded.
.SH PATHS
.B /
is the root,
.B /0
is its first child,
.B /0/2
is the third child of the first child. The indexes are 0\-based.
.SH VALUES
.TP
.BI hex: 4152
The bytes in hexadecimal; spaces and \- are ignored.
.TP
.BI utf8: TEXT
The UTF\-8 encoding of the text.
.TP
.BI ascii: TEXT
The ASCII encoding of the text.
.TP
.BI base64: QVI=
The bytes in base64.
.TP
.BI file: PATH
The content of a file.
.TP
.B empty
No content.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid command line: unknown command or option, missing argument, invalid path or value.
.TP
.B 2
The file or the node does not exist.
.TP
.B 3
The operation failed: invalid stream, existing file, deleting the root, I/O error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pedit new tree.prmt \-\-signature ascii:PRMT:DEMO
pedit add tree.prmt / \-\-data utf8:hello
pedit dump tree.prmt
pedit get tree.prmt /0 data \-\-format utf8
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1)
.PP
https://github.com/fuszenecker/Promptuarium
